From 5afa475e56e73bc94222541212aba271372de5fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fable <fable@local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:55:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] video_core: EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_SYNC, the first dispatches of a
 software matrix program run alone

The first run of Ocarina of Time's network on the console (EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact) has one
risk the code cannot remove: a dispatch that never ends on the one graphics queue, which RADV
turns into a device loss after 10 s without progress, and which has frozen the PS5 before. What
the emulator can do is keep nothing queued behind the unproven dispatch and say which one it was.

EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_SYNC=<n>: for the first n dispatches of a program with TensorMulAdd (Shader::Info
uses_software_matrix, net-01), DispatchCompute submits the command buffer right after recording
the dispatch and waits for the GPU on the GPU thread, logging "Software matrix dispatch i of n:
XxYxZ groups, GPU done after N ms". A dispatch that hangs stops in this wait; with
EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1 the stall report after 3 s names the compute pipeline, before the device
loss. A pipeline that is unbuilt or refused never gets here (EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_BACKGROUND sends
those to the stand-in first), so a wait that returns is a dispatch that ran. After n the program
runs as every other. Cost while watched: one GPU drain per dispatch, about one per frame.
Unset or 0: nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp         | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
index 5c2aa63..abeb8b0 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -1473,6 +1473,36 @@ void RasterizerVulkan::DispatchCompute() {
         cmdbuf.Dispatch(dim[0], dim[1], dim[2]);
     });
     SubmitNx2ListCopies();
+    // EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_SYNC=<n> (unset or 0: off): the first n dispatches of a software matrix
+    // program (Ocarina of Time's network, EDEN_NX2_TENSOR=compact) each run alone. The command
+    // buffer is submitted right after the dispatch and this thread waits for the GPU, so nothing
+    // is queued behind the dispatch while it is unproven, and each one logs its groups and its
+    // GPU time. A dispatch that never ends hangs in this wait: with EDEN_NX2_HANG_WATCH=1 the
+    // stall report after 3 s names the compute pipeline before RADV declares the device lost at
+    // 10 s. A refused or unbuilt pipeline never reaches here (EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_BACKGROUND, above),
+    // so a wait that ends is a dispatch that ran. After n dispatches the program runs unwatched.
+    static const u32 tensor_sync = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TENSOR_SYNC");
+        return value != nullptr ? static_cast<u32>(std::strtoul(value, nullptr, 10)) : 0U;
+    }();
+    if (tensor_sync != 0 && kepler_compute->IsNativeMode() && pipeline->UsesSoftwareMatrix()) {
+        static u32 synced{};
+        if (synced < tensor_sync) {
+            ++synced;
+            const auto start = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+            const u64 tick = scheduler.Flush();
+            scheduler.Wait(tick);
+            const double ms = std::chrono::duration<double, std::milli>(
+                                  std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - start)
+                                  .count();
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                     "Software matrix dispatch {} of {}: {}x{}x{} groups, GPU done after {:.1f} ms",
+                     synced, tensor_sync, dim[0], dim[1], dim[2], ms);
+            if (synced == tensor_sync) {
+                LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Software matrix dispatches run unwatched from here");
+            }
+        }
+    }
 
     // Log compute dispatch
     if (GPU::Logging::IsActive() &&
-- 
